// Title: Diamond Sleet APT Scheduled Task Creation - Registry
// Sigma ID: 9f9f92ba-5300-43a4-b435-87d1ee571688
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-10-24 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects registry event related to the creation of a scheduled task used by Diamond Sleet APT
//   during exploitation of Team City CVE-2023-42793 vulnerability
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2023/10/18/multiple-north-korean-threat-actors-exploiting-the-teamcity-cve-2023-42793-vulnerability/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules-emerging-threats/2023/TA/Diamond-Sleet/registry_event_apt_diamond_sleet_scheduled_task.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Schedule\\TaskCache\\Tree.*$" and RegistryKey contains "Windows TeamCity Settings User Interface"
